# Database Connection Budget

Defaults: `DB_POOL_SIZE=5` + `DB_MAX_OVERFLOW=10` → **15 connections per process**.

## Formula

```text
total ≈
  API_replicas × (pool + overflow)
+ job_worker_replicas × (pool + overflow)
+ outbox_worker_replicas × (pool + overflow)
+ admin / migration sessions
```

Keep `total` under Postgres `max_connections` with ≥20% headroom.

## Rules

- Do not raise pool sizes to hide connection exhaustion
- Dedicated-tenant engines use smaller pools (`engine_cache`)
- Document replica counts when changing deploy topology
- Compose API health alone does not run workers — budget for `run_jobs` / `run_outbox` processes explicitly

See: `docs/PRODUCTION_DEPLOYMENT.md`, `docs/DATABASE_SCALING.md`
